deepseek: "You are right to call that out. If an image can't communicate the **exact, precise, non-ambiguous logic** required for "polymath production grade" GregTech, then an image file is the wrong file type.

### The file that replaces an image file for this purpose is:

## The `.litematic` file
(Plus its companion text file: `.txt` or `.md`)

### Why `.litematic` (Litematica mod) beats any image file:

| Requirement | Image (PNG/JPG) | `.litematic` schematic |
|---|---|---|
| **Dimensions** | Visual estimate (15x15? 16x16? hard to see) | ✅ Exact block coordinates |
| **Machine placement** | Rough approximation | ✅ Every machine is placed exactly |
| **Spine layers** | Shown as a diagram | ✅ Placed in the world - no guessing Y-levels |
| **Pipes & cables** | Colored lines (guesswork) | ✅ Pre-routed (no spaghetti) |
| **Chunk alignment** | Overlay shown visually | ✅ Aligned to chunk borders automatically |
| **No abstract nonsense** | "Nonsensical words" (text boxes, labels) | ✅ No text, only blocks. See it, build it. |
| **Reusable** | Screenshot only (must rebuild manually) | ✅ Paste it instantly in-game |

---

### The Minimum Viable File Set for "Polymath Production Grade":

Instead of one image, you provide **two files**:

1.  **`gregtech_campus_layout_v1.litematic`** (The actual blueprint)
    - Contains the full Phase 2 Campus (all 5 buildings + spine + connections + chunk-aligned borders).
    - Player loads it in Litematica, sees a **ghost overlay**, builds it block-for-block without needing to interpret a diagram.

2.  **`gregtech_campus_layout_readme.txt`** (The "Polymath" companion text)
    - Contains the **throughput math** (mb/t, EU/t, items/sec).
    - Contains the **spine Y-level logic** (Y-4, Y-0, Y-2, Y-4).
    - Contains **chunk coordinates** (e.g., "Building 3 starts at chunk X: -15, Z: 27").
    - Contains **"Golden Rule" warning** ("This schematic is the 10x10. Build 3x bigger manually—Litematica does not scale").

---

